<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shigatse</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shigatse is the second-largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tibet">Tibet</a>, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsang">Tsang</a> region west of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lhasa">Lhasa</a>. It grew around the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shigatse-dzong">Samdrubtse</a>, seat of the Rinpungpa and Tsangpa rulers of Tsang in the 15th to 17th centuries. Its Tashilhunpo Monastery, founded in 1447, is the traditional seat of the Panchen Lamas.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/shigatse.jpg" alt="Shigatse" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Antoine Taveneaux · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Shigatse_Dzong.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
